# Reuse first

Before adding a helper, constant, type or schema, look for the existing one:

- `@pdf-insight/contracts`: payload schemas and types, request limits (`MAX_SCANNED_PAGES`,
  `MAX_PAGE_TEXT_LENGTH`, `MAX_IMAGE_BASE64_LENGTH`), ISO code lists, `API_ERROR_CODES`,
  `DOCUMENT_TYPES`, the id factories.
- `@pdf-insight/domain`: the ports, `isScannedPage`, `chunkPages`, `mergeAnalyses`,
  `numericTokens`, `groundAmounts`, `withOneRetry`, `AnalysisError` and its codes.
- `@pdf-insight/i18n`: the locales, `createTranslator`, `missingKeys`.
- `@pdf-insight/typescript-config` and `@pdf-insight/eslint-config`: extend them; never copy
  compiler or lint settings into a workspace.

Then:

- Search with `git grep` across `packages/` and `apps/` before writing anything shared.
- Parameterize the existing function (an options object, an injected dependency) rather than
  forking a near-copy of it.
- No parallel implementations: one schema per payload, one retry helper, one translator, one
  list of error codes. If the existing one is wrong, fix it in place, with a test, for every
  caller.
- What two workspaces need moves into the right package (a pure rule into `domain`, a shape
  into `contracts`), never into a copy in each app.
- Prefer the platform (`fetch`, `Intl`, `URL`) and the existing dependencies to a new library.
